   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 74 of the laws of 2020 relating to directing the\ndepartment of health to convene a work group on rare diseases, in relation to\nthe deadline to submit a report on rare diseases and to the effectiveness\nthereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5944",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5944-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§2 & 3, Chap 74 of 2020",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5944\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 74 of the laws of 2020 relating to directing the\ndepartment of health to convene a work group on rare diseases, in\nrelation to the deadline to submit a report on rare diseases and to the\neffectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo extend the deadline for the work group on rare diseases to submit a\nreport on rare diseases and the effectiveness thereof.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill extends the deadline for the department of\nhealth and rare disease workgroup to submit a report to the governor,\nspeaker of the assembly, and temporary president of the senate by one\nyear.\n\nSection two provides for the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2020, the legislature passed, and the Governor later chaptered 57172\nRivera/A9132 Paulin, which authorized the creation of a work group\nformed of experts in the field of rare diseases. The individuals in this\nwork group were tasked with examining how rare diseases are handled and\ntreated in New York State. Ultimately, the workgroup is required to\nproduce a report on their findings to help shape policy initiatives to\nimprove the lives of New Yorkers suffering from rare diseases.\n\nThe Department of Health (DOH), in collaboration with the department of\nfinancial services, was tasked with convening this workgroup.  However,\nDOH has been inundated with the State's response to COVID-19 and, as\nsuch, has not convened this workgroup.  This bill would extend the dead-\nline the workgroup has to submit a report on rare diseases to the Gover-\nnor, Speaker of the Assembly, and temporary President of the Senate by\none year. This extension would allow the workgroup to submit a report in\nDecember 2022, providing the workgroup with the time necessary to submit\na thorough and well-written report.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
