    "lawCode": "Amd §§2 & 3, Chap 74 of 2020",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5944A\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 74 of the laws of 2020 relating to directing the\ndepartment of health to convene a work group on rare diseases, in\nrelation to the deadline to submit a report on rare diseases and to the\neffectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo extend the deadline for the work group on rare diseases to submit a\nreport on rare diseases and the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill extends the deadline for the department of\nhealth and rare disease workgroup to submit a report to the governor,\nspeaker of the assembly, and temporary president of the senate by one\nyear. The bill also requires the workgroup to convene no later than\nDecember twentieth, 2021.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2020 the legislature passed, and the Governor later signed\nS.7172/A.9732 which authorized the creation of a work group formed of\nexperts in the field of rare diseases. The individuals in this work\ngroup were tasked with examining how rare diseases are handled and\ntreated in New York. Ultimately, the workgroup is required to produce a\nreport on their findings to help shape policy initiatives to improve the\nlives of New Yorkers suffering from rare diseases.\n\nThe Department of Health (DOH), in collaboration with the department of\nfinancial services, was tasked with convening this workgroup.  However,\nDOH has been inundated with the State's response to COVID-19 and, as\nsuch, has not had the capacity to convene this workgroup.\n\nThis bill would extend the deadline the workgroup has to submit a report\non rare diseases to the Governor, Speaker of the Assembly, and temporary\nPresident of the Senate by one year. This extension would allow the\nworkgroup to submit a report in December 2022, providing the workgroup\nwith the time necessary to submit a thorough and well-written report.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
